{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.SingleResult.error:Field","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","name":"error","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.SingleResult","kind":"field","sig_":"error : Error","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils.apply_while_list","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils","name":"apply_while_list","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T] apply_while_list(T, (T) -> T, (T) -> Bool) -> @list.List[T]","doc":"Repeatedly apply `f` starting from `x`, collecting every successor\n for which `cond` still holds. The first value (`x` itself) is *not*\n included; iteration stops the first time `cond(f(acc))` is false.\n\n **Order**: results are accumulated by prepending, so the list is\n returned in *reverse* iteration order — the last kept value first.\n A `halve-toward-zero` usage looks like\n\n     apply_while_list(16, z => z / 2, z => z > 0)\n     // yields [1, 2, 4, 8]   -- note: 1 is newest, 8 is oldest\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   debug_inspect(\n     apply_while_list(16, z => z / 2, z => z > 0),\n     content=(\n       #|<List: [1, 2, 4, 8]>\n     ),\n   )\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
