{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.unfold:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"unfold","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyList::unfold(Self[T], (Self[T]) -> (T, Self[T])?) -> Self[T]","doc":"Co-inductive dual of `fold_left`: given a step `f : LazyList -> (T, LazyList)?`,\n produce a lazy list by repeatedly applying `f` to the previous\n state. `f` returns `None` to terminate, otherwise `Some((elem, next_state))`.","attrs":[]}
