{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/laws.idempotent","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/laws","name":"idempotent","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/laws","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[A : Eq] idempotent((A) -> A) -> (A) -> Bool","doc":"Idempotent function.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyRef.from_thunk:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"from_thunk","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyRef","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyRef::from_thunk(() -> T) -> Self[T]","doc":"Wrap a delayed computation as a `LazyRef`. The thunk runs the first\n time `force` is called; subsequent forces return the cached value.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let mut runs = 0\n   let r = LazyRef::from_thunk(() => {\n     runs = runs + 1\n     \"hi\"\n   })\n   assert_eq(runs, 0)\n   assert_eq(r.force(), \"hi\")\n   assert_eq(r.force(), \"hi\")\n   assert_eq(runs, 1)\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.State.compute_size:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","name":"compute_size","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.State","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn State::compute_size(Self) -> Int","doc":"Pick the `size` argument to hand to the generator on the next\n draw. Grows with the number of successful tests so far (so later\n inputs are larger) while staying bounded by `max_test_size_`, and\n nudges up for every recently-discarded case so discards don't\n stall at a trivial size.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck.quick_check_silence","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","name":"quick_check_silence","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[P : @property.Testable] quick_check_silence(P, max_shrink? : Int, max_success? : Int, max_size? : Int, discard_ratio? : Int, expect? : @state.Expected, abort? : Bool, verbose? : Bool) -> String","doc":"Like `quick_check` but returns the formatted outcome as a `String`\n instead of printing it or raising. Useful in tests that want to\n pin the driver's output with `inspect(..., content=...)`.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.feat_random","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","name":"feat_random","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T : Enumerable] feat_random(Int) -> @gen.Gen[T]","doc":"Generate a value from an enumerable instance (up to a size bound).\n This is the Feat-backed random-sampling bridge: `gen` stays unaware\n of `Enumerable`, while `feat` can still produce ordinary generators.\n @alert unsafe \"Experimental: May cause stack overflow\"","attrs":[]}
