{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.map:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"map","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T, U] LazyList::map(Self[T], (T) -> U) -> Self[U]","doc":"Apply `f` to every element. Lazy — `map(f, xs).take(n)` only\n forces the first `n` cells.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let squared = infinite_stream(1, 1).map(x => x * x).take(4)\n   @debug.assert_eq(squared.iter().collect(), [1, 4, 9, 16])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
