{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils.removes_array","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils","name":"removes_array","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T] removes_array(Int, Int, Array[T]) -> Array[Array[T]]","doc":"Array-shaped counterpart of `removes_list`. Same chunk-wise\n semantics: emit one `xs[:i] ++ xs[i+k:]` per chunk boundary `i`,\n skipping the trailing chunk whose removal would leave the prefix\n unchanged.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   @debug.assert_eq(removes_array(2, 6, [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]), [\n     [3, 4, 5, 6],\n     [1, 2, 5, 6],\n   ])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils.const_","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils","name":"const_","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T, U] const_(T) -> (U) -> T","doc":"`const_(t)` is the constant function at `t`: it ignores whatever\n argument it receives and returns `t`. Typical use is currying away\n an unused parameter, e.g. `scale(const_(10))` fixes the size at 10.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let always_seven : (Int) -> Int = const_(7)\n   assert_eq(always_seven(0), 7)\n   assert_eq(always_seven(999), 7)\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/core/quickcheck.Arbitrary_for_moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedArray","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"moonbitlang/core/quickcheck.Arbitrary_for_moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedArray","parent":null,"kind":["impl","moonbitlang/core/quickcheck.Arbitrary","moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedArray"],"sig_":"pub impl[T : @quickcheck.Arbitrary + Compare] @quickcheck.Arbitrary for SortedArray[T]","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
