{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/report.TestError.NoneExpectedFail","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/report","name":"NoneExpectedFail","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/report.TestError","kind":"variant","sig_":"NoneExpectedFail(num_tests~ : Int, num_discarded~ : Int, coverage~ : @state.Coverage, output~ : String)","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink.Shrink","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink","name":"Shrink","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink","kind":"trait","sig_":"trait Shrink","doc":"Types that can enumerate \"smaller\" variants of a given value for\n the classical QuickCheck shrinker. Each call to `shrink(x)` returns\n an `Iter[Self]` of candidates strictly simpler than `x`; the driver\n walks these candidates after a failure, keeping the first one that\n still falsifies the property.\n\n The return type is `Iter[Self]` rather than `Array[Self]` so large\n or recursive shrink spaces stay lazy. The default body (`= _`)\n means \"no shrinks\" — a conservative starting point for types where\n shrinking isn't meaningful.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   // `Int` has a built-in Shrink instance that walks toward 0.\n   let candidates : Array[Int] = Shrink::shrink(100).collect()\n   assert_true(candidates.contains(0))\n   assert_true(candidates.length() > 0)\n   // `Bool` shrinks `true` to `false`, and `false` has no shrinks.\n   @debug.assert_eq(Shrink::shrink(true).collect(), [false])\n   @debug.assert_eq(Shrink::shrink(false).collect(), [])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.SingleResult.maybe_max_test_size:Field","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","name":"maybe_max_test_size","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.SingleResult","kind":"field","sig_":"maybe_max_test_size : Int?","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck.Arrow","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","name":"Arrow","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","kind":["type_alias","moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.Arrow"],"sig_":"pub using @property {type Arrow}","doc":"Re-export property/testable types from the lower-level property\n package.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink.Shrink_for_moonbitlang/core/uint64.UInt64","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink","name":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink.Shrink_for_moonbitlang/core/uint64.UInt64","parent":null,"kind":["impl","moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink.Shrink","moonbitlang/core/uint64.UInt64"],"sig_":"pub impl Shrink for UInt64","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyRef","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"LazyRef","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","kind":"type","sig_":"type LazyRef[T]","doc":"A mutable cell that memoises a thunk: it holds either an\n already-computed value or a delayed computation, and caches the\n result on first `force`. Used to make `LazyList` tails on-demand\n without recomputing them when traversed repeatedly.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck.label","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","name":"label","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","kind":["value_alias","function","moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.label"],"sig_":"pub fn[P : @property.Testable] label(P, String) -> @property.Property","doc":"Attaches a label to a test case.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck.Discard","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","name":"Discard","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","kind":["type_alias","moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.Discard"],"sig_":"pub using @property {type Discard}","doc":"Re-export property/testable types from the lower-level property\n package.","attrs":[]}
