{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.small_check_error_silence","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","name":"small_check_error_silence","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[A : Enumerable + @debug.Debug, B : @property.Testable] small_check_error_silence((A) -> B raise, max_size? : Int, expect? : @state.Expected, abort? : Bool, verbose? : Bool) -> String","doc":"Silent variant of `small_check_error`: returns the formatted\n outcome as a `String` instead of raising.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.Expected","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","name":"Expected","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","kind":"type","sig_":"enum Expected","doc":"What the *author* of a property *expects* to happen. This is the\n knob behind `quick_check_fn(..., expect=Fail)` and friends: if the\n driver's actual verdict matches `Expected`, the check is\n considered a pass even when the property raises.\n\n Use cases:\n\n - `Success` (the default) — property must hold on every generated\n   input.\n - `Fail` — the property *should* fail; useful when you want to\n   demonstrate a known bug or lock in a regression check. The test\n   fails if the driver *can't* find a counterexample.\n - `GaveUp` — the property is expected to discard too many cases.\n   Rarely useful in isolation; handy for testing the driver itself.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck.quick_check_fn_silence","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","name":"quick_check_fn_silence","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[A : @moonbitlang/core/quickcheck.Arbitrary + @shrink.Shrink + @debug.Debug, B : @property.Testable] quick_check_fn_silence((A) -> B, max_shrinks? : Int, max_success? : Int, max_size? : Int, discard_ratio? : Int, expect? : @state.Expected, abort? : Bool, verbose? : Bool) -> String","doc":"`quick_check_fn` variant that returns the formatted outcome as a\n `String` instead of raising / printing.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.NonEmptyList.not_equal:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"not_equal","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.NonEmptyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T : Eq] NonEmptyList::not_equal(Self[T], Self[T]) -> Bool","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.ArrowError","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property","name":"ArrowError","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property","kind":"type","sig_":"struct ArrowError[A, B]((A) -> B raise)","doc":"Same role as `Arrow`, but the wrapped function may `raise` an error.\n A raised error is converted into a failing property result.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.Expected","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property","name":"Expected","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property","kind":["type_alias","moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.Expected"],"sig_":"pub using @state {type Expected}","doc":"Re-export `Expected` from `internal/state` so lower-level property\n runners can spell run expectations without importing driver internals.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.Enumerate.add:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","name":"add","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.Enumerate","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] Enumerate::add(Self[T], Self[T]) -> Self[T]","doc":"`+` as an alias for `union`.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.UnicodeString.equal:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"equal","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.UnicodeString","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn UnicodeString::equal(Self, Self) -> Bool","doc":"automatically derived","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.ASCIIString.not_equal:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"not_equal","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.ASCIIString","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn ASCIIString::not_equal(Self, Self) -> Bool","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck.quick_check","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","name":"quick_check","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[P : @property.Testable] quick_check(P, max_shrink? : Int, max_success? : Int, max_size? : Int, discard_ratio? : Int, expect? : @state.Expected, abort? : Bool, verbose? : Bool) -> Unit raise Failure","doc":"Run a `Testable` property against randomly-generated inputs and\n print the outcome. The driver runs up to `max_success` successful\n tests, trying increasingly large inputs up to `max_size`, and\n discarding no more than `max_success × discard_ratio` inputs\n before giving up. On failure it shrinks for up to `max_shrink`\n steps before reporting.\n\n `expect` asserts the expected outcome (`Success` by default); the\n driver flips the verdict accordingly (a failing property with\n `expect=Fail` is a pass). `abort=true` short-circuits the outer\n loop after the first test result is processed — note that a\n failing result still goes through the full shrink search before\n returning.\n\n Raises `Failure` on mismatch with `expect` — so it's the\n drop-in entry point inside `test \"…\"` blocks.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.pay","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","name":"pay","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T] pay(() -> Enumerate[T]) -> Enumerate[T]","doc":"Shift every size class up by one: part `k` of `pay(f)` equals part\n `k - 1` of `f()`. The outer part `0` becomes empty. **This is the\n productivity knob** for recursive `Enumerable` instances — every\n recursive self-reference must be wrapped in `pay` or the fixpoint\n diverges.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/testing.enqueue","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/testing","name":"enqueue","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/testing","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn enqueue(Queue, Int) -> Queue","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Positive.shrink:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"shrink","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Positive","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn Positive::shrink(Self[Int]) -> Iter[Self[Int]]","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink.Shrink.shrink:Field","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink","name":"shrink","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink.Shrink","kind":"field","sig_":"shrink(Self) -> Iter[Self]","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck.Shrink","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","name":"Shrink","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","kind":["trait_alias","moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink.Shrink"],"sig_":"pub using @shrink {trait Shrink}","doc":"Re-export the `Shrink` trait so existing callers can keep writing\n `@quickcheck.Shrink` after the trait's definition moved to the\n `moonbitlang/quickcheck/shrink` subpackage.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.Property.classify:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property","name":"classify","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.Property","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn Property::classify(Self, Bool, String) -> Self","doc":"Method form of `classify`, useful for chaining property decorators.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.State.add_coverages:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","name":"add_coverages","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.State","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn State::add_coverages(Self, SingleResult) -> Unit","doc":"Fold the labels / classes carried by `res` into the running\n `Coverage` tally. Called after each passing test so the final\n report can print label-and-class percentages.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.from_config","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","name":"from_config","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn from_config(Config) -> State","doc":"Build a fresh `State` from the caller-supplied caps. All counters\n start at zero, `expected` defaults to `Success`, and the PRNG is\n seeded from `@splitmix.new()`.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/core/builtin.Eq_for_moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Negative","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"moonbitlang/core/builtin.Eq_for_moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Negative","parent":null,"kind":["impl","moonbitlang/core/builtin.Eq","moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Negative"],"sig_":"pub impl[T : Eq] Eq for Negative[T]","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/core/debug.Debug_for_moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Blind","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"moonbitlang/core/debug.Debug_for_moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Blind","parent":null,"kind":["impl","moonbitlang/core/debug.Debug","moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Blind"],"sig_":"pub impl[T] @debug.Debug for Blind[T]","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedList.arbitrary:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"arbitrary","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T : @quickcheck.Arbitrary + Compare] SortedList::arbitrary(Int, @splitmix.RandomState) -> Self[T]","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.Finite","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","name":"Finite","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","kind":"type","sig_":"struct Finite[T]","doc":"A finite chunk of `T` values, represented compactly as a\n cardinality plus an indexer rather than as a stored collection.\n No values are materialised until `fIndex` is called.\n\n Fields:\n - `fCard`: number of elements (≥ 0). Zero denotes the empty chunk.\n - `fIndex`: `(i : BigInt) -> T`, total on `[0, fCard)`.\n\n `Finite[T]` is the basic building block used by `Enumerate[T]`:\n one part per size class. The combinators below give it a ring-like\n algebra (disjoint union, Cartesian product, maps, fmap).","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.SingleResult.abort:Field","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","name":"abort","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.SingleResult","kind":"field","sig_":"abort : Bool","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen.frequency","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen","name":"frequency","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T] frequency(Array[(UInt, Gen[T])]) -> Gen[T]","doc":"Chooses one of the given generators, with a weighted random distribution.\n @alert unsafe \"Panics if the array is empty or total weight is zero\"\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   // 90% chance of \"common\", 10% chance of \"rare\". With a fixed seed\n   // the draws are deterministic — over 10 samples we expect mostly\n   // \"common\".\n   let g = frequency([(9U, pure(\"common\")), (1U, pure(\"rare\"))])\n   for x in g.samples() {\n     assert_true(x == \"common\" || x == \"rare\")\n   }\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.add:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"add","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyList::add(Self[T], Self[T]) -> Self[T]","doc":"`+` as an alias for `concat`.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.to_lazy","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"to_lazy","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T] to_lazy(@list.List[T]) -> LazyList[T]","doc":"Promote an eager `@list.List[T]` to its lazy counterpart. The\n resulting `LazyList` has its tails in `LazyRef::from_value` form,\n so no delayed computation is involved — just a type conversion.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let xs : LazyList[Int] = to_lazy(@list.from_array([1, 2, 3]))\n   @debug.assert_eq(xs.iter().collect(), [1, 2, 3])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.LazyList","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","name":"LazyList","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","kind":["type_alias","moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList"],"sig_":"pub using @lazy {type LazyList}","doc":"A call-by-need list: either empty (`Nil`) or a head value paired\n with a thunk producing the rest (`Cons(head, LazyRef<tail>)`).\n Because the tail is a `LazyRef`, infinite lists (`repeat`,\n `infinite_stream`) are representable and cheap — only the prefix\n you iterate is forced.","attrs":[]}
