{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.concat:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"concat","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyList::concat(Self[T], Self[T]) -> Self[T]","doc":"Lazy append. `(xs.concat(ys)).take(n)` only forces as many cells\n as are consumed; the right-hand list is not touched until the left\n runs out.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let xs : LazyList[Int] = from_list(@list.from_array([1, 2]))\n   let ys : LazyList[Int] = from_list(@list.from_array([3, 4]))\n   @debug.assert_eq(xs.concat(ys).iter().collect(), [1, 2, 3, 4])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
