{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen.one_of","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen","name":"one_of","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T] one_of(Array[Gen[T]]) -> Gen[T]","doc":"Randomly uses one of the given generators.\n @alert unsafe \"Panics if the array is empty\"\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let g = one_of([pure(1), pure(2), pure(3)])\n   for x in g.samples() {\n     assert_true(x == 1 || x == 2 || x == 3)\n   }\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Positive.equal:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"equal","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.Positive","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T : Eq] Positive::equal(Self[T], Self[T]) -> Bool","doc":"automatically derived","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.split_at:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"split_at","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyList::split_at(Self[T], Int) -> (Self[T], Self[T])","doc":"Split at index `i`: returns `(take(i), drop(i))` in a single pass.\n The prefix is eagerly collected; the suffix stays lazy.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let xs : LazyList[Int] = from_list(@list.from_array([1, 2, 3, 4]))\n   let (lhs, rhs) = xs.split_at(2)\n   @debug.assert_eq(lhs.iter().collect(), [1, 2])\n   @debug.assert_eq(rhs.iter().collect(), [3, 4])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyRef.from_value:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"from_value","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyRef","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyRef::from_value(T) -> Self[T]","doc":"Promote an already-evaluated value to a `LazyRef`. `force` on the\n result returns immediately without computing anything.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let r = LazyRef::from_value(7)\n   assert_eq(r.force(), 7)\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
