{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.tails:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"tails","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyList::tails(Self[T]) -> Self[Self[T]]","doc":"All suffixes of the list, starting with `self` itself and ending\n with `Nil`. The outer result is also a `LazyList`, so `tails` is\n safe to apply to an infinite input — only the suffixes you inspect\n are forced.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let xs : LazyList[Int] = from_list(@list.from_array([1, 2, 3]))\n   let lens = xs.tails().iter().map(t => t.length()).collect()\n   @debug.assert_eq(lens, [3, 2, 1, 0])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.Enumerate.at:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat","name":"at","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/feat.Enumerate","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] Enumerate::at(Self[T], @bigint.BigInt) -> T","doc":"Return the `i`-th value overall: walk parts from size 0 upward,\n subtracting each part's cardinality from `idx` until `idx` falls\n inside the current part, then read the value via `fIndex`.\n\n **Aborts** on out-of-range indices (reaches `Nil`).\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let bools : Enumerate[Bool] = Enumerable::enumerate()\n   assert_eq(bools[0], true)\n   assert_eq(bools[1], false)\n }\n ```","attrs":[["alias",["op_name","_[_]"],false],["alias",["name","en_index"],true]]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.forall","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property","name":"forall","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T : Testable, A : @debug.Debug] forall(@gen.Gen[A], (A) -> T) -> Property","doc":"Run with an explicit generator.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/core/builtin.Eq_for_moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedArray","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"moonbitlang/core/builtin.Eq_for_moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedArray","parent":null,"kind":["impl","moonbitlang/core/builtin.Eq","moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedArray"],"sig_":"pub impl[T : Eq] Eq for SortedArray[T]","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
