{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.UnicodeString.not_equal:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"not_equal","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.UnicodeString","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn UnicodeString::not_equal(Self, Self) -> Bool","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.take:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"take","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyList::take(Self[T], Int) -> Self[T]","doc":"First `n` elements (or fewer, if the list is shorter). Lazy in the\n tail — subsequent cells aren't forced unless requested.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let nats : LazyList[Int] = infinite_stream(0, 1)\n   @debug.assert_eq(nats.take(3).iter().collect(), [0, 1, 2])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.State.max_test_size_:Field","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state","name":"max_test_size_","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/state.State","kind":"field","sig_":"mut max_test_size_ : Int","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
