{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/rose.Rose.fmap:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/rose","name":"fmap","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/rose.Rose","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T, U] Rose::fmap(Self[T], (T) -> U) -> Self[U]","doc":"Map `f` over every node in the tree, preserving structure. The\n result has the same shape as `self`, with each node's value\n replaced by `f(value)`.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let tree = @rose.Rose(1, [pure(2), pure(3)].iter())\n   let doubled = tree.fmap(x => x * 2)\n   @debug.assert_eq(doubled.iter().collect(), [2, 4, 6])\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
