{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen.Gen.bind:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen","name":"bind","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen.Gen","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T, U] Gen::bind(Self[T], (T) -> Self[U]) -> Self[U]","doc":"Monad instance for Gen[T]\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   // Use bind to sequence generators: first pick `n`, then draw an\n   // `n`-element list of the fixed value 0.\n   let g = pure(3).bind(n => pure(0).list_with_size(n))\n   debug_inspect(\n     g.sample(),\n     content=(\n       #|<List: [0, 0, 0]>\n     ),\n   )\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedList.not_equal:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers","name":"not_equal","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/modifiers.SortedList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T : Eq] SortedList::not_equal(Self[T], Self[T]) -> Bool","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.index:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"index","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyList::index(Self[T], Int) -> T","doc":"Return the element at position `i`. **O(n)** — walks the list from\n the head. Aborts if `i` is negative or past the end.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let xs : LazyList[Int] = from_list(@list.from_array([10, 20, 30]))\n   assert_eq(xs.index(0), 10)\n   assert_eq(xs.index(2), 30)\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList.drop_while:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy","name":"drop_while","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/lazy.LazyList","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T] LazyList::drop_while(Self[T], (T) -> Bool) -> Self[T]","doc":"Skip the longest prefix where `p` holds and return the rest. Forces\n cells while `p` is true; the suffix starting at the first failure\n stays lazy.","attrs":[]}
