{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/laws.Equivalence.bind:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/laws","name":"bind","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/laws.Equivalence","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn[T, U] Equivalence::bind(Self[T], (T) -> Self[U]) -> Self[U]","doc":"Monadic bind on an `Equivalence`: `f(lhs).lhs` and `f(rhs).rhs`.\n Asymmetric on purpose — each side threads through its own\n transformation, so you can lock in \"left follows left, right\n follows right\" under a further algebra step.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.Discard.property:Method","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property","name":"property","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/property.Discard","kind":"method","sig_":"pub fn Discard::property(Self) -> Property","doc":null,"attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils.removes_list","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils","name":"removes_list","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/internal/utils","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T] removes_list(Int, Int, @list.List[T]) -> @list.List[@list.List[T]]","doc":"Chunk-wise removal for list shrinkers.\n\n Given `xs` of length `n`, walk it in blocks of `k` and emit one\n variant per non-empty tail chunk, each variant formed by\n concatenating the prefix seen so far with the suffix after the\n dropped chunk:\n\n     removes_list(2, 6, [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])\n     == [[3, 4, 5, 6], [1, 2, 5, 6]]\n\n The final chunk is never a variant — removing it would leave the\n list unchanged on the prefix side. When `k > n` the result is empty.\n\n Part of the classical QuickCheck list shrinker: combining the\n outputs for different chunk sizes produces a \"halve toward empty\"\n shrinking strategy.\n\n ```mbt check\n test {\n   let xs = @list.from_array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])\n   debug_inspect(\n     removes_list(2, 6, xs),\n     content=(\n       #|<List: [<List: [3, 4, 5, 6]>, <List: [1, 2, 5, 6]>]>\n     ),\n   )\n }\n ```","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck.quick_check_fn_error_silence","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","name":"quick_check_fn_error_silence","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[A : @moonbitlang/core/quickcheck.Arbitrary + @shrink.Shrink + @debug.Debug, B : @property.Testable] quick_check_fn_error_silence((A) -> B raise, max_shrinks? : Int, max_success? : Int, max_size? : Int, discard_ratio? : Int, expect? : @state.Expected, abort? : Bool, verbose? : Bool) -> String","doc":"`quick_check_fn_error` silent variant that returns the formatted\n outcome as a `String`.","attrs":[]}
{"key":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen.one_of_list","pkg":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen","name":"one_of_list","parent":"moonbitlang/quickcheck/gen","kind":"function","sig_":"pub fn[T] one_of_list(@list.List[T]) -> Gen[T]","doc":"Randomly uses one of the given generators in list\n @alert unsafe \"Panics if the list is empty\"","attrs":[]}
